\begin{remarks}
    \begin{remark}
        For the full model setup, we mainly showed that \name{} family, especially \arosink{} performs competively; but it did not showed better performance than hybrid setup. In fact, in \Cref{subsec: Exp Sigma-MoE} we will further push to a 2B-parameter model $+$ 8$\times$ over-train scale, and show that at the first $1\times$ Chinchilla law regime, full model training indeed performs worse; however, when we continue to over-train the model, full model training with \name{} started to outperform its hybrid versions, and gives the best performance. 
    \end{remark}
\end{remarks}

\begin{takeaways}
    \textbf{Takeaways for \Cref{exp: gpt}: on large-scale pretraining tasks with GPT2-XL-1.5B, \name{} (especially \arosink{}) significantly outperforms both AdamW and Muon, and makes full model training a viable option.}
\end{takeaways}







