\sum_{n \geq 0} |a_{n,m}| \frac{p_n}{q_m} &\leq N\qquad\text{ for any }m.
\end{align*}
Then, $T:l^2(\N) \rightarrow l^2(\N)$ defined by $(Tx)_n=\sum_{m \geq 0} a_{n,m} x_m$ is well-defined bounded linear operator and $\norm{T}\leq \sqrt{MN}$.
