Here, $\delta_{1,\dots,n}=\otimes_{i=1}^n v_i$, where $\{v_1,\dots,v_n\}$ is the canonical basis of $\R^n$. The process $\mathbf{Z}^{\epsilon,i_1,\dots,i_n}$ (respectively, $\mathbf{W}^{i_1,\dots,i_n}$) denotes the canonical rough path lift of $\left(\phi^{\epsilon}_{i_1}\ast W^{i_1,\H},\dots,\phi^{\epsilon}_{i_n}\ast W^{i_n,\H}\right)$ (respectively, $\left(W^{i_1,\H},\dots,W^{i_n,\H}\right)$).\\
