presented on the middle picture.
Observe that the reconstructed curve has a shallower dent
than the original, making it appear longer. This is a reminiscent of the problem: how would a string wrapped around the Earth equator
rise if the string was extended by 10 cm?
The right picture of Figure \ref{fig6.1} shoes the velocity vector, i.e., the curve
$s\mapsto\frac{d\gamma(s)}{ds}$, where $s$ is the arc length.
The loops formed by the velocity vector correspond to zones where the curvature of $\gamma$ changes its sign.

