All presented schemes preserve boundedness as shown in Fig.~\ref{sol2:minmax2}. The
\femL scheme preserves the bounds due to the limiter, but has an issue with increased
mass deviation as previously noted. A cause for this could be the use of the Taylor-Hood
elements and \fem which are not necessarily divergence-free as highlighted in Rem.~\ref{rem:RT}.
Moreover, since the governing equation is solved using \fem we therefore do not have
a flux-treatment for the velocity field $\mathbf{u}$ over the boundaries, which is
present for the other studied schemes \sipgL, \swipL, and \asu.  \par
 Finally, energy dissipation is obtained for all schemes as shown in Figs.~\ref{fig:ac2eneg}
and \ref{fig:ac2eneg2}. Furthermore, we note that even though the energy curves in
