Now, the formal definition given in~\ref{YMFormula} gives perfect sense as a random distributional $1-$form on $\mathcal{S}$. The next theorem shows that the parallel transport generated by this $1-$form verifies the Driver--Sengupta formula.


\begin{thm}[Driver--Sengupta Formula]
    The random $1-$form $A$ defined in~\ref{YMFormula} induces via stochastic differential equations, on any graph on $\Sigma$ whose edges are either flow lines or level sets, holonomies verifying the Driver--Sengupta formula. 
\end{thm}
