An important observation of the previous lemma is that the law of $H_{N;k}$ knowing $\mathcal{F}_{\leq j}$ is only a function of $H_{N;j}$, not of all the bonds situated under the level set $j2^{-N}$. Therefore, we conclude the following lemma. 
\begin{lemma}
    We have, for any central function,
    $\mathbb{E}[f(H_{N;k})|\mathcal{F}_j]=\mathbb{E}[f(H_{N;k})|H_{N;j}].$
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Direct consequence of the previous lemma.
