This section presents the numerical evaluation of the proposed multi-fidelity,
multi-objective optimization framework. The analysis covers four main aspects:
(i) assessment of the reduced-order design space generated by PD--PME,
(ii) surrogate accuracy across fidelity levels,
(iii) convergence of the multi-objective search, and
(iv) characterization of the obtained optimal configuration relative to the
baseline manta-inspired geometry.

