Gas flow across nodes is governed by so-called \emph{coupling conditions} that come in the form of algebraic equations, cf. \cite{BandaHertyKlar2006,Gas-Modell:DomschkeHillerLangTischendorf2017,KochEtAl2015}. For gas mixtures, these coupling conditions typically involve the following assumption:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
